Need update prev at end after all assignments. But if we use `leadPump` output directly, could read it? We'll use internal maybe, but output assigned. At end we set prevLead := leadPump; etc. This uses outputs; in ST, reading output variables is allowed in most systems? The standard allows reading output variables like ordinary variables. To be safer, we can store outputs in local variables `newLead`, `newLag`, `newRunCount` and assign outputs at end. But property expects outputs cycle end. Could do:
